==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|over-}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ofer-}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*uber}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*upér}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|over-}}, {{cog|de|über-}}, {{cog|sv|över-}}, {{cog|cy|gor-}}, {{cog|es|sobre-}}, {{cog|hy|վեր-}}, {{cog|fa|ابر}} (''abar-''). {{doublet|en|super-|sur-|hyper-}}. More at {{l|en|over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈəʊ̯.vəɹ/}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈəʊ̯.və/|[ˈəʊ̯və]|a=RP}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈoʊ̯.vɚ/|[ˈʌ̝ʊvɚ]|a=GA}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈɐʉ̯.və/|[ˈɐʉ̯vɐ]|a=NZ,AU}}
** {{IPA|en|[ˈo̝.vər]|a=Scottish English}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈoː.bʱə(ɾ)/|a=Indian English}}

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# {{senseid|en|above or higher}}[[above|Above]], or [[high#Adjective|higher]].
#: {{m|en|overbar}}, {{m|en|overlook}}
# {{senseid|en|superior}} [[superior#Adjective|Superior]].
#: {{m|en|overlord}}
# {{senseid|en|excessively}} [[excessive|Excessive]]; [[excessively]].
#: {{m|en|overkind}}, {{m|en|overloud}}, {{m|en|overstate}}
# {{senseid|en|surrounding or covering}} [[surrounding#Adjective|Surrounding]] or [[covering#Adjective|covering]].
#: {{m|en|overcoat}}, {{m|en|overpaint}}
# {{senseid|en|extremely or intensely}} {{lb|en|augmentative}} [[exceptional|Exceptional]]; [[extremely]] or [[intensely]].

====Usage notes====
Comparison of relative combinations (two separate words, hyphenated or a single compound word) does not easily fit a pattern; terms become compound words as they are broadly accepted.

